oup":"Civil Aircraft Operators and Air Carriers"},{"effect":"Must adhere to new interagency agreements regarding ADS-B Out usage, implement manned rotary-wing safety management systems, conduct risk assessments for special missions, and maintain transponders every 90 days.","group":"Department of Defense and Military Personnel"},{"effect":"Subject to new time-on-position limits for supervisors, mandatory scenario-based training on threat/error management and visual separation, and new safety risk assessment tools.","group":"Air Traffic Controllers"}],"key_provisions":["Requires the FAA to issue rules mandating collision prevention technology (including ADS-B In) for covered civil aircraft, with a final compliance deadline no later than December 31, 2031.","Requires the Department of Defense (DOD) and Department of Transportation to enter into an agreement ensuring DOD helicopters use ADS-B Out as default in national airspace and are equipped with integrated collision prevention technology by December 31, 2031.","Prohibits operations on a specific segment of Helicopter Route 4 between Hains Point and the Woodrow Wilson Memorial Bridge.","Mandates that the FAA establish new training programs for air traffic controllers regarding threat and error management and visual separation procedures.","Requires the DOT Inspector General to audit the safety culture and safety management systems of the FAA's Air Traffic Organization and Aviation Safety Management Organization."],"missing_information":["Exact financial costs and appropriations required to implement the mandated technological upgrades across civilian and military fleets are not specified in the text."],"plain_summary":"The ALERT Act addresses aviation safety in response to the January 29, 2025 midair collision near Ronald Reagan Washington National Airport. It introduces new mandates and timelines for collision avoidance technology, such as ADS-B In and ACAS Xa/Xr, across civil aircraft, rotorcraft, and Department of Defense aircraft. It also requires the FAA and Department of Defense to update air traffic control procedures, training, safety management systems, route planning, and coordination protocols.","significance":"The ALERT Act represents a sweeping legislative response to a major aviation disaster, enacting extensive technological mandates, operational reforms, and interagency coordination requirements across both civil aviation and military airspace management."},"summary_meta":{"generated_at":"2026-10-25T11:43:24+00:00","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","source_basis":"text+summary","source_urls":["https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr7613/BILLS-119hr7613rfs.htm"]},"summary_threshold":50,"title":"ALERT Act","viability":76.1,"viability_detail":{"breakdown":[{"available":true,"effective_weight":35.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Detected stage","value":"Passed one chamber"}],"key":"stage","label":"Legislative stage","note":"Stage value from the table on the About page.","points":28.0,"value":0.8,"weight":35},{"available":true,"effective_weight":15.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Committee activity","value":"Reported out of committee (or past committee stage)"}],"key":"committee","label":"Committee activity","note":"","points":15.0,"value":1.0,"weight":15},{"available":true,"effective_weight":15.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Floor activity","value":"Passed a chamber"}],"key":"floor","label":"Floor consideration","note":"","points":15.0,"value":1.0,"weight":15},{"available":true,"effective_weight":15.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Days since latest action","value":193},{"label":"Half-life (days)","value":90}],"key":"momentum","label":"Recent action","note":"","points":3.39,"value":0.2262,"weight":15},{"available":true,"effective_weight":10.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Cosponsors","value":87},{"label":"House majority","value":218}],"key":"cosponsors","label":"Cosponsorship","note":"","points":6.32,"value":0.6317,"weight":10},{"available":true,"effective_weight":10.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Democratic supporters","value"